<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <title>Privacy Policy</title>
    <link rel="icon" href="others/assets/relic.webp" />
    <link
      href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@300;400;500;700&display=swap"
      rel="stylesheet"
    />
    <style>
      * {
        margin: 0;
        padding: 0;
        box-sizing: border-box;
      }

      body {
        font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;
        background: #0a0e1a;
        color: #d4d4d4;
        line-height: 1.7;
        padding: 15px;
      }

      .container {
        max-width: 850px;
        margin: 0 auto;
        background: #13182b;
        border-radius: 6px;
        padding: 35px 45px;
        border: 1px solid #1e2840;
      }

      h1 {
        color: #6ba3ff;
        font-size: 2.2em;
        margin-bottom: 8px;
        font-weight: 600;
      }

      .last-updated {
        color: #6b7280;
        font-size: 0.85em;
        margin-bottom: 35px;
      }

      h2 {
        color: #7fb8ff;
        font-size: 1.6em;
        margin-top: 35px;
        margin-bottom: 12px;
        font-weight: 600;
      }

      h3 {
        color: #9bc9ff;
        font-size: 1.15em;
        margin-top: 18px;
        margin-bottom: 8px;
        font-weight: 500;
      }

      p {
        margin-bottom: 12px;
        color: #c7c7c7;
      }

      ul {
        margin-left: 25px;
        margin-bottom: 12px;
        list-style: disc;
      }

      li {
        margin-bottom: 6px;
        color: #c7c7c7;
      }

      a {
        color: #5b9fff;
        text-decoration: underline;
      }

      a:hover {
        color: #7fb8ff;
      }

      .back-button {
        display: inline-block;
        margin-top: 25px;
        padding: 10px 24px;
        background: #2563eb;
        color: #fff;
        border-radius: 4px;
        text-decoration: none;
        font-weight: 500;
        font-size: 0.95em;
        margin-right: 8px;
      }

      .back-button:hover {
        background: #1d4ed8;
      }

      .section {
        margin-bottom: 20px;
      }

      .info-box {
        background: #1a2336;
        border-left: 3px solid #3b82f6;
        padding: 14px;
        margin: 18px 0;
      }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <script>
      sessionStorage.setItem('privacy_visited', 'true');
    </script>
    <div class="container">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="last-updated">updated jan 24 2026</p>

      <div class="section">
        <p>
          We're not here to spy on you. This policy explains what data we
          actually collect (spoiler: not much) and what we do with it.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="info-box">
        <strong>The Short Version:</strong> We collect basically nothing. Your
        settings live on your device, we use Google ads to keep the lights on,
        and Firebase counts how many people are online. That's it. We don't sell
        anything.
      </div>

      <h2>1. What We Actually Collect</h2>
      <div class="section">
        <h3>Automatic Stuff</h3>
        <p>When you visit, we automatically see some basic tech info:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>What browser you're using</li>
          <li>Your operating system and screen size</li>
          <li>Which pages you look at</li>
          <li>Your IP address (but it's anonymized)</li>
        </ul>
        <p>This is just standard web stuff that every site sees.</p>

        <h3>What's Saved On Your Device</h3>
        <p>Your browser saves your Aether preferences locally:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Your theme choice</li>
          <li>Tab cloaking settings</li>
          <li>Recently played games</li>
          <li>Panic button settings</li>
          <li>Whether you want the snow effect on or off</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          This stuff never leaves your device. It's all stored in your browser's
          local storage. You can nuke it anytime through browser settings or the
          "Clear Cache" button.
        </p>

        <h3>Firebase Counter</h3>
        <p>
          We use Firebase to show the "X users online" thing on the homepage.
          That's literally all it does - counts active sessions anonymously.
        </p>

        <h3>What We DON'T Collect</h3>
        <p>Just to be clear:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            No names, emails, or personal info (there's no accounts anyway)
          </li>
          <li>No passwords or payment info (the site is free)</li>
          <li>No tracking what sites you visit through the seearch</li>
          <li>No detailed browsing history</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <h2>2. How We Use This Info</h2>
      <div class="section">
        <p>The minimal data we collect helps us:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Keep the site running</li>
          <li>Make sure it works on different browsers</li>
          <li>Show how many people are currently online</li>
          <li>Fix bugs when they pop up</li>
          <li>Display ads (that's how we pay for hosting)</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <h2>3. Third-Party Services</h2>
      <div class="section">
        <h3>Ad</h3>
        <p>
          We use Google ads. They track stuff to show relevant ads. You can opt
          out of personalized ads at
          <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" target="_blank"
            >Google Ads Settings</a
          >.
        </p>
        <p>
          More info:
          <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads" target="_blank"
            >How Google uses data</a
          >
        </p>

        <h3>Firebase</h3>
        <p>
          Firebase handles the online user counter. It's run by Google. Their
          privacy policy:
          <a href="https://firebase.google.com/support/privacy" target="_blank"
            >Firebase Privacy</a
          >
        </p>

        <h3>Games & Apps</h3>
        <p>
          Third-party games and apps have their own privacy policies. We don't
          control those.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h2>4. Search Privacy</h2>
      <div class="section">
        <p>The search feature:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            We don't log what sites you visit
            <b>DOESNT MEAN YOUR SCHOOL CANT</b>
          </li>
          <li>We don't store any data from sites you access</li>
          <li>Your search usage isn't tied to any identifier</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          <strong>Heads up:</strong> Your school/work network can still
          potentially see your traffic depending on their setup. The search feature hides
          it from the sites you visit, not necessarily from your network admin.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h2>5. Cookies & Tracking</h2>
      <div class="section">
        <p>Here's what tracks you:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Local Storage:</strong> Saves your settings on your device
            forever (until you clear it)
          </li>
          <li><strong>Google Ads Cookies:</strong> For showing ads</li>
          <li>
            <strong>Firebase:</strong> For counting users during your session
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          You can disable cookies in your browser settings, but some stuff might
          break.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h2>6. Security</h2>
      <div class="section">
        <p>
          We try to keep things secure with HTTPS and minimal data collection.
          But nothing on the internet is 100% secure, so keep that in mind.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h2>7. Kids</h2>
      <div class="section">
        <p>
          If you're under 13, you shouldn't be here. We don't knowingly collect
          data from anyone under 13. If you're 13-17, get your parents'
          permission before using the site.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h2>8. Your Rights</h2>
      <div class="section">
        <p>You can:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>See your local data through browser dev tools</li>
          <li>Delete everything with the "Clear Cache" button in settings</li>
          <li>Opt out of personalized ads through Google</li>
          <li>Block analytics with browser extensions</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Since most data lives on your device anyway, you've got full control.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h2>9. How Long We Keep Stuff</h2>
      <div class="section">
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Local Storage:</strong> Forever, until you delete it</li>
          <li>
            <strong>Firebase Stats:</strong> Whatever Firebase's default
            retention is
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Server Logs:</strong> 30 days max for security purposes
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <h2>10. International Use</h2>
      <div class="section">
        <p>
          The site is hosted in the US. If you're accessing from somewhere else,
          your data might pass through US servers. By using Aether, you're cool
          with that.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h2>11. Do Not Track</h2>
      <div class="section">
        <p>
          Some browsers have a "Do Not Track" feature. We don't really respond
          to it since we're barely tracking anything anyway.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h2>12. Policy Changes</h2>
      <div class="section">
        <p>
          This policy might get updated. Check back occasionally. The "Last
          Updated" date at the top tells you when we last changed something.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h2>13. California Residents</h2>
      <div class="section">
        <p>
          CCPA gives you extra rights if you're in California. We don't sell
          personal info, so most of this doesn't apply. But you've got the right
          to know what we collect (covered above) and request deletion (use the
          Clear Cache button).
        </p>
      </div>

      <h2>14. European Users</h2>
      <div class="section">
        <p>
          GDPR gives you rights like accessing your data, deleting it, and
          opting out. Most of your data is on your device, so you already have
          control. For the rest, use the features built into the site.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h2>15. Questions?</h2>
      <div class="section">
        <p>Got questions? Use the feedback options on the site.</p>
      </div>

      <div style="margin-top: 40px">
        <p>
          <strong
            >we collect as little as possible. most of it lives on your device
            anyway.</strong
          >
        </p>
        <a href="/index.html" class="back-button">← back home</a>
        <a href="tos.html" class="back-button">terms</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </body>
</html>
"} };
  var XHTML = "http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml";
